        <headline>DUTY TSRV - BLEED AND PRESSURISATION</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: 
ACMS REVIEW CARRIED OUT FOLLOWING A DUAL PNEUMATIC EVENT NOTIFICATION. ACMS HAS BEEN REVIEWED FOR RYR 26ZX FROM LPL-TFS, SHOWING LHS BLEED SYSTEM DOES NOT EXCEED 26 PSI IN ANY FLIGHT PHASE. DURING DESCENT, 10.51 PSI IS NOTED ON LHS AND 13.50 PSI ON RHS BOTH PRESSURE VALUES ARE MOMENTARY AND STRONG RECOVERY IS MADE. 

ACMS REVIEW HAS FOUND LHS PRESSURE LOW ON ALL STAGES OF THE FLIGHT. FURTHER INVESTIGATION REQUIRED.  

HEALTH CHECK REQUIRED

ACTION:  

1. GAIN ACCESS TO THE #1 BLEED COMPONENTS.  

2. USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #1 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.

* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM

** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.  

3. INSPECT ALL SYSTEM SENSE LINES AND CONNECTIONS FOR ANY SIGNS OF DAMAGE, BLOCKAGE OR LEAKAGE. MAKE THE NECESSARY RECTIFICATIONS.
 
4.CHECK  DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE PN 16135-81 FOR OBSTRUCTION USING COMPRESSED NITROGEN.
 
5. LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. SPECIAL FOCUS ON  THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES OR FITTINGS:
   A) PRSOV DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE
   B) SENSE LINES BETWEEN BAR AND PCCV
   C) SUPPLY SENSE LINE TO HSR
   D) SENSE LINE TO PRSOV
   E) SENSE LINE TO 450 SENSOR
   F) 390 SENSOR SENSE LINES FROM PCCV UNION
 
6. CLOSELY INSPECT LH PRSOV FOR NOTCHY BEHAVIOUR, INABILITY TO REMAIN OPEN AND ACTUATOR BODY LEAKAGE.
 
7. CHECK BLEED AIR REGULATOR FOR D/S PORT LEAKAGE OR RUPTURED REVERSE FLOW DIAPHRAGM
 
8. REPLACE ANY FAULTY COMPONENT FOUND IAW AMM, IF NFF CHANGE THE PRSOV IAW IAW AMM 36-11-04/401.
 
9. RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICE.
 
**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.  
 
**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
